What this solution actually does: SWF_OUT_ETL is a timer-driven Windows service that prepares the outgoing SWIFT messages produced by the T24 core before they are handed to the sender. The tracked appsettings.json shows a 30,000 ms interval, but the host reads its real interval from the encrypted central configuration, so the production value is not visible here (appsettings.json:1-12 (../../SWIFT/Outgoing/SWF_OUT_ETL/SWF_OUT_ETL/appsettings.json#L1-L12), ServiceHost.cs:72-83 (../../SWIFT/Outgoing/SWF_OUT_ETL/SWF_OUT_ETL/ServiceHost.cs#L72-L83)). On every tick the service loads the system date and ten system parameters, checks the business day and the operating-hours window and then reads the operations whose status is READ (IT24/008 SP usp_SwfOutEtl_GetOperacionesEtl.sql:29-43 (../../StoredProcedures/MWD_DB/DBMDW/SWIFT/Outgoing/SWF_OUT_ETL/IT24/Procedures/008%20SP%20usp_SwfOutEtl_GetOperacionesEtl.sql#L29-L43)). For each operation it: (1) normalizes the T24 message text and extracts the SWIFT header and block 4 with one regular expression (OperacionServicio.cs:336-352 (../../SWIFT/Outgoing/SWF_OUT_ETL/Aplicacion_ETL/OperacionServicio.cs#L336-L352), OperacionServicio.cs:386-423 (../../SWIFT/Outgoing/SWF_OUT_ETL/Aplicacion_ETL/OperacionServicio.cs#L386-L423)); (2) parses every tag against the syntax rows (des_regexp) stored in the database (OperacionServicio.cs:654-737 (../../SWIFT/Outgoing/SWF_OUT_ETL/Aplicacion_ETL/OperacionServicio.cs#L654-L737)); (3) resolves the destination BIC with the rule for the message type (MT103, MT199, MT202/MT202COV, MT400, MT410, MT412, MT700 or the default rule; for MT940/MT950 from the configured destinations) and rewrites the header and tags (53A/54A, 56A, 57D, the 50/59 format and the {121:} UETR) (OperacionServicio.cs:742-839 (../../SWIFT/Outgoing/SWF_OUT_ETL/Aplicacion_ETL/OperacionServicio.cs#L742-L839)); (4) persists the control and detail rows (tb_srv_swf_out_control, tb_srv_swf_out_detail) and the rewritten message (NF_MQ_MSG_ETL) (PersistenciaSwiftService.cs:37-101 (../../SWIFT/Outgoing/SWF_OUT_ETL/Aplicacion_ETL/Servicios/PersistenciaSwiftService.cs#L37-L101)); (5) validates the account and the customer against the T24 views (CoreValidatorService.cs:306-369 (../../SWIFT/Outgoing/SWF_OUT_ETL/Aplicacion_ETL/Servicios/CoreValidatorService.cs#L306-L369)); (6) accepts the operation (status X_ASR, variables XML and core fields written) or rejects it (X_ASR with the manual flag) and e-mails the configured recipients (OperacionServicio.cs:947-962 (../../SWIFT/Outgoing/SWF_OUT_ETL/Aplicacion_ETL/OperacionServicio.cs#L947-L962)); and (7) inserts the folio into the AutomationHeap queue (procedure usp_SwfOutEtl_InsQueueLaikaHeap) for the downstream sender (OperacionServicio.cs:913-931 (../../SWIFT/Outgoing/SWF_OUT_ETL/Aplicacion_ETL/OperacionServicio.cs#L913-L931), IT24/013 SP usp_SwfOutEtl_InsQueueLaikaHeap.sql:46-97 (../../StoredProcedures/MWD_DB/DBMDW/SWIFT/Outgoing/SWF_OUT_ETL/IT24/Procedures/013%20SP%20usp_SwfOutEtl_InsQueueLaikaHeap.sql#L46-L97)). All database access goes through stored procedures (22 usp_SwfOutEtl_* definitions plus one T24-view procedure are kept in the database repository) and the T24 account and customer data comes through the shared ConexionT24Mw views. The service therefore edits payment instructions, not only moves rows: a defect in the header, tag or validation logic changes what the bank sends.
