False-positive checks were resolved as follows:
• No C# 8 or later syntax is used in the production projects: Aplicacion_ETL and Infraestructura_ETL set no LangVersion (they default to C# 7.3 for net48) and the host pins 7.3, so the missing LangVersion is not a build risk; only the test project selects LangVersion latest and uses newer syntax such as null!.
• No string-built SQL, SQL injection or XML injection path exists: every call passes values through CrearParametro, and XmlBuilderHelper writes values as DOM text nodes (XmlBuilderHelper.cs:57-69 (../../SWIFT/Outgoing/SWF_OUT_ETL/Aplicacion_ETL/Helpers/XmlBuilderHelper.cs#L57-L69)).
• Configuracion.Pid is nullable, but the host reads it only after ObtenerProcesoActualAsync has set it (ServiceHost.cs:143-147 (../../SWIFT/Outgoing/SWF_OUT_ETL/SWF_OUT_ETL/ServiceHost.cs#L143-L147)) and AppLogger dereferences it inside its own try/catch (AppLogger.cs:57-75 (../../SWIFT/Outgoing/SWF_OUT_ETL/Infraestructura_ETL/Comun/AppLogger.cs#L57-L75)), so no nullable-PID defect exists today (GEN-8 does not apply; the latent risk is in ETL-FR-33).
• The Ñ, Ç and ñ characters in the ConstantesSwift keys are deliberate: NormalizarCampo maps . to Ñ, / to Ç and the digit 5 to ñ (StringHelper.cs:26-35 (../../SWIFT/Outgoing/SWF_OUT_ETL/Aplicacion_ETL/Helpers/StringHelper.cs#L26-L35)), so they are not an encoding artifact; only their cryptic, non-invertible design is noted in ETL-FR-27.
• The {4: regular expression requires CRLF line breaks, but the pipeline first replaces the T24 line-break marker with Environment.NewLine (OperacionServicio.cs:343 (../../SWIFT/Outgoing/SWF_OUT_ETL/Aplicacion_ETL/OperacionServicio.cs#L343)), so CRLF is the intended input contract on Windows.
• An empty UETR is not expected: the shared GeneraSwEnd2EndRef always returns a new GUID (T24MwEnd2End.cs:41-70 (../../General/MUFGT24_BTMUM_64/MUFG_T24/Infraestructura/Repositorios/T24/T24MwEnd2End.cs#L41-L70)); the defects around {121:} are the double insertion and the ignored update result (ETL-FR-10).
• The error e-mail does not block the tick: CorreoHelper.EnviarCorreo returns a Task<bool> (CorreoHelper.cs:39-42 (../../General/MUFGT24_BTMUM_64/MUFG_T24/Infraestructura/Correo/CorreoHelper.cs#L39-L42)). The defect is that the task is not awaited and its result is ignored (ETL-FR-13).
• ReglaMT103 renames 50K to 50F and 59 to 59F without reformatting; the code documents it as the legacy "forzar formato F" behavior (ReglaMT103.cs:91-101 (../../SWIFT/Outgoing/SWF_OUT_ETL/Aplicacion_ETL/Reglas/Implementaciones/ReglaMT103.cs#L91-L101)), so it is not ticketed.
• All FirstOrDefault() results are either null-guarded or used on lists, and the two First() calls are guarded by Count == 1 and ContainsKey, so no InvalidOperationException on an empty sequence was found.
Items that need business or owner confirmation before the corresponding fix is finalized:
• A production sample of the T24 message as stored in nf_mq_msg and of the message the downstream sender expects in NF_MQ_MSG_ETL: whether the header rewrite, the {121:} insertion and the 54A/57D replacement are meant to operate on the full FIN message or on block 4 only (ETL-FR-1, ETL-FR-10 and ETL-FR-11).
• Whether the deployed database contains usp_SwfOutEtl_GetListSwiftOutFields under that name, and how usp_SwfOutEtl_GetFinancialInstitutionRelationForCurrency is called successfully with its three OUTPUT parameters (ETL-FR-44 and ETL-FR-45).
• The intended meaning of the statuses READ, X_ASR, RECC and PROC and whether an operation in error is meant to be retried on every tick without limit (ETL-FR-2 and ETL-FR-3).
• Whether MT940/MT950 and MT202COV are processed by this service in production, and who maintains the destination rows for them (ETL-FR-16 and ETL-FR-35).
• Whether a decimal comma can reach the MONEY parameter of usp_SwfOutEtl_UpdQualifyAuto (SELECT CAST('1234,50' AS money) is expected to return 123450.00 and should be confirmed with a one-line test), the Windows regional setting of the service account and the production values of the date/time parameters (ETL-FR-8).
• The real timer interval and the unit of TamanoMaximoArchivoLogKB passed to Logging.Init (the shared method multiplies its argument by 1,024 as if it were megabytes; ETL-FR-38).
• Whether FinancialInstitutionRelations.IsPreferred is meant to sort ascending in usp_SwfOutEtl_GetFinancialInstitutionRelationForCurrency (ETL-FR-45), and whether another process allocates references from tb_srv_t24_swf_ctl_folios (ETL-FR-46).
• Whether the T24 account currency to compare is CURRENCY or ACCOUNT_CURRENCY (ETL-FR-9).
